Z||000000||FieroSTETZ||10-03-2001||03:04 AM||||since i have been unable to find a 1977 celica GT, i am looking at buying a 2002 celica GTS - test drove one, but auto (and dealer was with me) anyone have any feedback?<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.shawnrocks.com/Animation1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Fformula88||10-03-2001||12:11 PM||||My friends father has a GTS, very sweet car.  I love the cockpit feel of them!  I suppose more low end torque would be nice, but the 6-speed lets you build revs quick enough to get to the high HP.  It also handles very well.  From everything I have heard, do NOT get a GTS auto.  I have even read a number of reviews that have stated your better off with the GT if you want an auto.  The GTS engine isn't a good match I guesss... the auto must not be geared to keep it in the pper RPM range.<P>I'd also suggest taking a look at the new Acura RSX-Type S.  I like its cleaner exterior styling a little more, and it gives you 4/50 warrenty as opposed to 3/36.  Otherwise they both are probably very similar.  The RSX gives 20 more horses, but is a little heavier too.  IMO, these two come down to personal taste/preference.  ||||reg||1
