Z||000009||Fformula88||10-04-2001||09:56 AM||||You mean the Challenger show car?  They don't sell anything badged Challenger... and the last thing they did was a crap two door K-Car anyway.  Or do you mean the new Stratus coupes?  I like their styling too, again clean lines.  None of this "new edge" crap.  But they are technically re-badged Mitsu Eclipses with a stretched body (maybe wheelbase too?)  But its the same Eclipse engines and trannies... and an identical interior!!  Kind of sad Dodge didn't put enough money into the car to distinguish the inside a little better.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Jaei Sun||10-04-2001||11:21 AM||||Yeah the new Stratus/Sebring Coupes use the 3.0 v6 Mitsu ~200 HP.  I'm wondering why Chrysler didn't use their new 2.7 v6 allum ~200 HP in the cars?<P>I think the Stratus/Sebring coupes look a hellva lot better than their Eclipse couterparts.  This isn't the first time Dodge just rebodied the outside and left the interior alone of a Mitsu---- the 3kGT / Stealth for example.<P>||||reg||1
